Stock-level stacked column chart of annual site energy consumption in TBtu comparing the ComStock baseline against the Packaged GHP upgrade, with per-segment values printed inside the bands and column totals above: Baseline 4338 TBtu and Packaged GHP 3831 TBtu, a 507 TBtu (11.7%) reduction. The legend spans 17 fuel-and-end-use categories, from Heat Rejection and Heat Recovery Electricity through Pumps, Refrigeration, Exterior Lighting, the Water Systems categories (Other Fuel, District Heating, Natural Gas, Electricity), the Heating categories (Other Fuel, District Heating, Natural Gas, Electricity), Interior Lighting, Cooling (District Cooling, Electricity), Fans, and Interior Equipment (Natural Gas, Electricity). Labeled segments that change: Cooling Electricity falls from 667.3 to 534.7 (132.6 TBtu saved, 19.9%), Heating Electricity rises from 175.2 to 250.8 (a 75.6 TBtu increase, 43.2%), and Fans Electricity rises from 519.1 to 541.5 (22.4 TBtu, 4.3%). The large hatched red Heating Natural Gas band falls by 455.2 TBtu (53.2%), and Pumps Electricity rises by 25.1 TBtu (58.9%). Unaffected segments are identical in both columns: Interior Equipment Electricity 739.7, Interior Equipment Natural Gas 212.1, Interior Lighting Electricity 451.9. Total heating load across all fuels falls 37%.
